{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "_comment": [
    "How a battle looks, apart from what it does. Units play one clip per action (idle, walk, attack, hit, death) named <clips>.<action>;",
    "every skill reuses the unit's attack clip, and the skill itself is shown by an effect picture (the old-Pokemon way): fx.* clips from clips.json.",
    "units.<id>.impact_frame: the attack frame where the blow lands (effects and the target's reaction start then).",
    "skills.<id>.kind: impact = plays on every unit reached | projectile = flies from the caster, then plays `impact` | zone = plays on every covered cell.",
    "Optional per skill: scale, impact_scale, lift (px above the cell centre), speed (projectile px/s), stagger (s between targets), lunge (px the caster steps in),",
    "rotate (turn a projectile toward its heading), ground (draw under units), from_sky (projectile falls onto its target).",
    "A skill without an entry uses default_effect. Clips are built by tools/anim/build_sheets.py."
  ],
  "move_seconds": 0.22,
